('127.392.d.8.A',4,'To measure the voltage drop across a resistor, connect the voltmeter:','["after the load", "only to ground", "in series with it", "in parallel with it"]'::jsonb,3,'Voltmeters connect across components.','original'),
('127.392.d.8.B',3,'A generator works on the principle of:','["electromagnetic induction", "gravity feed", "friction heat", "chemical reaction"]'::jsonb,0,'Moving conductors in a field induce voltage.','original'),
('127.392.d.8.B',4,'Transformers lose some energy as heat in the:','["plug cover", "core and windings", "case paint", "label"]'::jsonb,1,'Core and winding losses produce heat.','original'),
('127.392.d.8.C',3,'A simple voltage divider is built from two:','["wires only", "diodes", "resistors", "switches"]'::jsonb,2,'Two series resistors divide voltage.','original'),
('127.392.d.8.C',4,'To limit current through an LED powered from a battery, a designer adds a:','["bigger LED", "parallel capacitor", "second battery", "series resistor"]'::jsonb,3,'The resistor sets a safe current.','original')
