('127.393.d.3.B',3,'A milestone in a project schedule marks:','["a random delay", "a lunch break", "an employee birthday", "a significant completed point"]'::jsonb,3,'Milestones show key achievements.','original'),
('127.393.d.3.B',4,'The sequence of tasks that determines the shortest possible project duration is the:','["critical path", "short circuit", "main street", "longest wire"]'::jsonb,0,'Delays on the critical path delay the project.','original'),
('127.393.d.3.C',3,'Operating a simulated electronics company gives students experience in:','["only repairing cars", "production and marketing roles", "only sports", "no business skills"]'::jsonb,1,'Simulated firms mirror real company functions.','original'),
('127.393.d.3.C',4,'In a student-run enterprise, quality control staff are responsible for:','["buying lunches", "hiring the teacher", "inspecting products before sale", "setting prices only"]'::jsonb,2,'QC checks products meet standards.','original'),
('127.393.d.3.D',3,'Before building a product, a production plan should include a:','["guess at success", "coin toss", "random sketch", "list of required materials and steps"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans list materials and procedures.','original'),
('127.393.d.3.D',4,'Estimating how long each assembly step takes helps a planner to set:','["a realistic production schedule", "a company logo", "a color theme", "a price tag only"]'::jsonb,0,'Time estimates drive scheduling.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.A',3,'A work order for a repair typically records the customer''s request, the work done, and:','["the technician''s pets", "parts used", "the weather", "the stock price"]'::jsonb,1,'Work orders document labor and parts.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.A',4,'Completed work orders are kept as records to:','["avoid billing", "reduce quality", "document services and costs", "hide mistakes"]'::jsonb,2,'Records support billing and accountability.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.B',3,'Which factor most directly affects the cost of manufacturing an electronic device?','["The CEO''s age", "The color of the box only", "The name of the product", "Cost of components and labor"]'::jsonb,3,'Parts and labor drive manufacturing cost.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.B',4,'Ordering components in larger quantities often lowers the cost per part because of:','["volume discounts", "tariffs only", "delays", "inflation"]'::jsonb,0,'Suppliers discount bulk orders.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.C',3,'A project budget estimates:','["only the weight", "the total cost of materials and labor", "the end date only", "only the profit"]'::jsonb,1,'Budgets forecast project costs.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.C',4,'If a project''s actual costs exceed its budget, the team should:','["ignore the overrun", "hide the numbers", "identify the cause and adjust the plan", "double the scope"]'::jsonb,2,'Variance analysis leads to corrective action.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.D',3,'A production schedule helps a company make sure orders are:','["delayed on purpose", "lost", "never filled", "completed on time"]'::jsonb,3,'Schedules coordinate delivery.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.D',4,'Scheduling assembly steps in order of dependency means a step starts only after:','["its prerequisite steps are done", "it is canceled", "the product ships", "everything else is lost"]'::jsonb,0,'Dependent tasks wait for their predecessors.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.E',3,'A patent protects an inventor''s:','["pay rate", "invention from being copied", "lunch hours", "office space"]'::jsonb,1,'Patents give exclusive rights to an invention.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.E',4,'Using a copyrighted software library in a product without a license may violate:','["gravity", "zoning rules", "copyright law", "tax tables"]'::jsonb,2,'Software is protected by copyright.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.F',3,'A service manual often contains a schematic, a parts list, and:','["jokes", "poetry", "recipes", "troubleshooting steps"]'::jsonb,3,'Manuals guide repair work.','original'),
('127.393.d.4.F',4,'To read a technical drawing correctly, you must first understand its:','["symbols and notes", "paper brand", "author''s hobbies", "file date only"]'::jsonb,0,'Symbols and notes carry the meaning.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.A',3,'Why do advanced electronics students still take safety tests?','["Hazards disappear with skill", "Higher voltages and complex equipment add hazards", "Tests are optional", "Tests replace labs"]'::jsonb,1,'Advanced work involves greater risks.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.A',4,'A passing safety test score shows that a student:','["is an expert", "owns the lab", "knows the rules for safe equipment use", "can ignore the rules"]'::jsonb,2,'It verifies safety knowledge.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.B',3,'Before servicing a power supply, the manual will tell you to:','["spray it with water", "remove the ground pin", "plug it in", "disconnect it from mains power"]'::jsonb,3,'De-energize before servicing.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.B',4,'Safety labels and instructions on equipment must be:','["read and followed", "ignored", "covered up", "removed"]'::jsonb,0,'Labels warn of real hazards.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.C',3,'OSHA''s lockout/tagout standard is intended to prevent:','["slow payroll", "unexpected startup of equipment", "paint damage", "noise complaints"]'::jsonb,1,'LOTO protects workers during servicing.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.C',4,'The National Electrical Code (NEC) provides rules for:','["traffic flow", "menu planning", "safe electrical installations", "dress codes"]'::jsonb,2,'The NEC governs wiring safety.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.D',3,'Cathode ray tubes and fluorescent bulbs may contain:','["cotton", "food dyes", "gold bars", "lead or mercury"]'::jsonb,3,'Older electronics contain toxic metals.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.D',4,'Waste that is toxic, corrosive, ignitable, or reactive is classified as:','["hazardous waste", "general trash", "recyclable paper", "compost"]'::jsonb,0,'These traits define hazardous waste.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.E',3,'Lithium batteries should be taken to:','["a creek", "a battery recycling site", "the incinerator at home", "the kitchen sink"]'::jsonb,1,'Lithium cells can start fires if mishandled.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.E',4,'Hazardous waste records, called manifests, track waste from the generator to:','["a retail store", "the front office", "its final disposal site", "the cafeteria"]'::jsonb,2,'Manifests document cradle-to-grave handling.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.F',3,'A technician checks a soldering station''s temperature setting regularly to:','["change wire color", "add flux", "lower the voltage", "ensure safe, quality joints"]'::jsonb,3,'Correct temperature prevents bad joints and damage.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.G',3,'An ESD wrist strap protects components by:','["draining static charge safely", "heating parts", "adding voltage", "building up charge"]'::jsonb,0,'The strap bleeds off static.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.G',4,'Moisture-sensitive ICs are often stored in sealed bags with:','["water", "desiccant", "tape", "oil"]'::jsonb,1,'Desiccant absorbs moisture.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.H',3,'Skipping scheduled maintenance on test equipment can result in:','["free repairs", "improved accuracy", "inaccurate measurements", "longer warranties"]'::jsonb,2,'Drift goes uncorrected without maintenance.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.H',4,'A technician who knowingly uses damaged safety equipment could be considered:','["careful", "heroic", "exempt", "negligent"]'::jsonb,3,'Knowingly ignoring hazards is negligence.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.A',3,'Mesh analysis uses which law to write equations for each loop?','["Kirchhoff''s voltage law", "Newton''s law", "Kirchhoff''s current law", "Faraday''s law"]'::jsonb,0,'Mesh equations sum loop voltages.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.A',4,'Nodal analysis is based on:','["Lenz''s law", "Kirchhoff''s current law", "Kirchhoff''s voltage law", "Boyle''s law"]'::jsonb,1,'Node equations sum currents at junctions.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.B',3,'In a purely resistive AC circuit, voltage and current are:','["90 degrees apart", "unrelated", "in phase", "opposite always"]'::jsonb,2,'Resistors do not shift phase.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.B',4,'In a series RC circuit, the time constant is found by multiplying:','["inductance by frequency", "voltage by current", "power by time", "resistance by capacitance"]'::jsonb,3,'Tau = R x C.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.C',3,'A voltage regulator is used to:','["keep an output voltage steady", "stop current", "create energy", "raise noise"]'::jsonb,0,'Regulators hold a constant output.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.C',4,'A Zener diode regulator works by operating the diode in:','["open circuit", "reverse breakdown", "forward bias only", "saturation only"]'::jsonb,1,'Zeners hold voltage in reverse breakdown.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.D',3,'A diode allows current to flow mainly when it is:','["overheated", "unpowered", "forward biased", "reverse biased"]'::jsonb,2,'Forward bias lets current pass.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.D',4,'A transistor used as a switch operates between cutoff and:','["regulation", "induction", "oscillation", "saturation"]'::jsonb,3,'Switching uses the off and fully-on states.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.E',3,'A rectifier circuit changes:','["AC to pulsating DC", "light to sound", "DC to AC", "heat to current"]'::jsonb,0,'Rectifiers convert AC to DC.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.E',4,'In a power supply, the filter capacitor reduces:','["wire size", "ripple voltage", "diode count", "input power"]'::jsonb,1,'Filtering smooths the rectified output.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.F',3,'In optoelectronics, a photodiode differs from an LED because it:','["stores charge", "amplifies sound", "converts light into current", "emits light"]'::jsonb,2,'Photodiodes detect light.','original'),
('127.393.d.6.F',4,'An optocoupler is used to:','["heat a wire", "amplify audio", "join two circuits'' grounds", "electrically isolate two circuits"]'::jsonb,3,'Light carries the signal across an isolation gap.','original'),
