('127.393.d.7.B',3,'A logic analyzer is used to examine:','["body temperature", "paint thickness", "digital signals", "water quality"]'::jsonb,2,'Logic analyzers capture digital states.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.B',4,'A spectrum analyzer displays signal strength versus:','["shelf life", "wire gauge", "paint color", "frequency"]'::jsonb,3,'Spectrum analyzers show amplitude across frequency.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.C',3,'A scope probe set to 10x reduces the signal at the scope by a factor of:','["ten", "one thousand", "hundred", "two"]'::jsonb,0,'A 10x probe attenuates by ten.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.C',4,'To avoid damaging a circuit when measuring with an analog meter, you should start on:','["the lowest range", "the highest range", "the resistance range", "a random range"]'::jsonb,1,'Start high, then reduce range.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.D',3,'A transient simulation shows how a circuit''s voltages change over:','["color", "distance", "time", "cost"]'::jsonb,2,'Transient analysis plots values versus time.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.D',4,'Before trusting a simulation result, a designer should:','["delete the file", "ignore the model", "avoid tests", "compare it with real measurements"]'::jsonb,3,'Models must be validated.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.E',3,'The component that stores data permanently in a computer, even when power is off, is the:','["hard drive or SSD", "power cord", "cooling fan", "RAM chip"]'::jsonb,0,'Drives are non-volatile storage.','original'),
('127.393.d.7.E',4,'The motherboard''s main role is to:','["produce power", "connect and allow communication among components", "protect from viruses", "store the monitor"]'::jsonb,1,'The motherboard links the parts.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.A',3,'A schematic page divided into functional blocks, such as power and control sections, is easier to:','["erase", "print", "read and troubleshoot", "lose"]'::jsonb,2,'Block organization aids understanding.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.A',4,'On a multi-sheet schematic, off-page connectors show that a net:','["ends at the page edge", "is broken", "is grounded", "continues on another sheet"]'::jsonb,3,'Off-page connectors link sheets.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.B',3,'Using redundant power supplies in critical equipment is a way to design in:','["reliability", "clutter", "noise", "weight"]'::jsonb,0,'Redundancy keeps systems running.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.B',4,'Adding overvoltage protection to a design primarily improves:','["only cost", "safety and reliability", "only weight", "only appearance"]'::jsonb,1,'Protection prevents damage and hazards.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.C',3,'Replacing a bulky linear regulator with a switching regulator can improve a product''s:','["heat output", "weight", "efficiency", "fragility"]'::jsonb,2,'Switchers waste less power.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.C',4,'Customer complaints about short battery life suggest a redesign focused on:','["louder buttons", "brighter paint", "bigger logos", "lower power consumption"]'::jsonb,3,'Reducing consumption extends battery life.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.D',3,'Industry-standard schematics use symbols defined by organizations such as:','["IEEE and IEC", "USDA and FDA", "NASA and NATO", "NFL and NBA"]'::jsonb,0,'IEEE and IEC publish symbol standards.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.D',4,'A title block on a schematic typically includes the drawing''s name, date, and:','["phone ringtone", "revision number", "lunch order", "weather"]'::jsonb,1,'Revision control is part of the title block.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.E',3,'Before filing for a patent, an inventor usually performs a:','["cooking class", "weather study", "prior art search", "tax audit"]'::jsonb,2,'The search checks whether the idea is new.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.E',4,'In the U.S., patent applications are filed with the:','["Weather Service", "Postal Service", "Forest Service", "Patent and Trademark Office"]'::jsonb,3,'The USPTO examines patents.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.F',3,'Designers use CAD software to lay out a printed circuit board by placing parts and:','["routing traces", "cooking meals", "painting walls", "adding ads"]'::jsonb,0,'Traces connect component pads.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.F',4,'Before ordering a printed circuit board, a designer runs a design rule check to find:','["spelling mistakes", "spacing and connection errors", "price changes", "color issues"]'::jsonb,1,'DRC catches layout errors.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.G',3,'Wireless power transfer, such as charging a phone without a cable, is an example of:','["an outdated method", "a hand tool", "an innovative technology", "a fuse type"]'::jsonb,2,'Wireless charging is a newer approach.','original'),
('127.393.d.8.G',4,'Wearable electronics are an emerging field because they combine sensors with:','["large heavy tubes", "unpowered paper", "steam engines", "small, low-power electronics"]'::jsonb,3,'Wearables need compact, efficient circuits.','original'),
('127.393.d.9.A',3,'After designing a circuit and building a prototype, the next step is to:','["test it against requirements", "sell it immediately", "discard the design", "stop work"]'::jsonb,0,'Testing checks the prototype meets requirements.','original'),
('127.393.d.9.A',4,'Prototypes are built in stages, such as breadboard, perfboard, and then:','["a final sale", "a printed circuit board", "a lunch table", "a drawing only"]'::jsonb,1,'PCBs are the refined stage.','original'),
('127.393.d.9.B',3,'A reflow oven is used to:','["paint boards", "drill metal", "solder surface-mount parts", "cut wire"]'::jsonb,2,'Reflow melts solder paste.','original'),
('127.393.d.9.B',4,'For fine surface-mount work, a technician often uses:','["a ladder", "a sledgehammer", "a garden hose", "a microscope and tweezers"]'::jsonb,3,'Small parts need magnification and precision.','original'),
('127.393.d.9.C',3,'When presenting a prototype to a panel, you should be prepared to:','["explain design choices and test results", "hide failures", "avoid questions", "skip the demo"]'::jsonb,0,'Panels expect justification and data.','original'),
('127.393.d.9.C',4,'A prototype demonstration is most convincing when it:','["has no data", "shows the product meeting its stated requirements", "is delayed", "hides its limits"]'::jsonb,1,'Meeting requirements proves success.','original'),
('127.391.d.9.G',4,'Which pictorial drawing type shows the front face in true shape, with depth lines drawn at an angle?','["Orthographic drawing", "Isometric drawing", "Oblique drawing", "Section drawing"]'::jsonb,2,'Oblique drawings keep the front face undistorted.','original'),
('127.392.d.5.G',4,'A heater is rated 1,200 watts at 120 volts. How much current does it draw?','["0.1 amps", "1,320 amps", "144,000 amps", "10 amps"]'::jsonb,3,'I = P / V = 1200 / 120 = 10 A.','original'),
('127.393.d.3.A',4,'Which project management phase involves the team doing the work described in the plan?','["Executing", "Planning", "Closing", "Initiating"]'::jsonb,0,'Executing carries out the plan.','original'),
('127.393.d.5.F',4,'Which routine task keeps a bench power supply''s readings trustworthy?','["Unplugging daily", "Periodic calibration", "Swapping knobs", "Painting the case"]'::jsonb,1,'Calibration verifies accuracy.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
